-- title:
--   Inertia of order at most 3 at supersingular chart primes
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ with $5 \le p$ and $M \ge 5$ with $p \nmid M$, a characteristic-zero field $L$ that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ for $\{p\}$, and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$. Let $K_1, K_2$ be intermediate fields of $L \subseteq L((q))$: $K_1$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion field $\mathbb{Q}$-field of $\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(p)$, and $K_2$ likewise for $\Gamma_0(Mp)$, with $K_2 \le K_1$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, containing $\zeta$ and with $p$ in its maximal ideal, which is generated by $\varpi$, with compatible $A$-algebra structures on $K_1$ and $K_2$; let $j \in K_1$ and $j_2 \in K_2$ be nonzero elements whose Laurent expansions are both the image of the $q$-expansion of the modular $j$-invariant. Over the two-chart integral models — the pushouts of the spectra of the subalgebras $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}$ and $\mathrm{chartAlgInf}$ of elements integral over $A[j]$, resp. $A[j^{-1}]$ — assume given a morphism $\pi_2$ from the model of $(A, K_1, j)$ to that of $(A, K_2, j_2)$ together with an $A$-algebra map $\iota_{F_2}$ between the finite chart algebras inducing the identity on Laurent series, such that: $\pi_2$ commutes with the structure morphisms to $\operatorname{Spec} A$; $\operatorname{Spec} \iota_{F_2}$ followed by the chart immersion of the $K_2$-model equals the chart immersion of the $K_1$-model followed by $\pi_2$; the $\pi_2$-preimage of the open range of the $K_2$-chart immersion is the open range of the $K_1$-chart; $\pi_2$ and $\iota_{F_2}$ are finite; and an element of $K_1$ lies in the finite chart algebra of the $K_1$-model exactly when it is integral over the image of $\iota_{F_2}$ inside it. Let $z$ be a point of the $K_1$-model at which the germ of the global section coming from $\varpi$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and let $y$ be a point of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the finite chart algebra mapping to $z$, supersingular in the sense that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $p$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the finite chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel the prime of $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,p\,\Omega$, i.e. every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero affine point killed by $p$. Finally let $G$ be a finite group acting faithfully by semiring automorphisms on $K_1$, fixing precisely the elements whose Laurent series lies in $K_2$ (both directions assumed), and acting on the finite chart algebra compatibly with its action on $K_1$. Then, for $\mathfrak{y}$ the prime ideal of $y$, the inertia subgroup $\mathfrak{y}.\mathrm{inertia}\ G = \{g \in G : g \cdot a - a \in \mathfrak{y} \text{ for all } a\}$ has cardinality at most $3$.
--
--   This bounds the ramification of the diamond-type group $G$ with fixed field the $X_0(Mp)$-field at a supersingular point of the characteristic-$p$ fibre of the integral model of $X(\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(p))$, the bound $3$ reflecting the possible extra automorphisms of a supersingular $j$-invariant for $p \ge 5$. It feeds the companion result asserting that this inertia group is cyclic of order prime to $p$ (tameness).
